= = = Jean Baudrillard = = =
Jean Baudrillard (27 July 1929 – 6 March 2007) was a French sociologist, philosopher and cultural theorist.
= = = Pierre Mendès France = = =
Pierre Isaac Isidore Mendès France (11 January 1907 – 18 October 1982), known as PMF, was a French politician who served as President of the Council of Ministers (equivalent in the French Fourth Republic to Prime Minister) for eight months from 1954 to 1955.
France died on October 18, 1982 in Paris, France at the age of 75.
= = = Alfred Kastler = = =
Alfred Kastler (3 May 1902 – 7 January 1984) was a French physicist. In 1966, he won the Nobel Prize in Physics.
= = = Chatham Borough, New Jersey = = =
Chatham is a borough in Morris County, New Jersey, United States. As of the 2020 United States Census, Chatham's population was 9,212.
= = = Natalia LL = = =
Natalia Lach-Lachowicz (18 April 1937 – 12 August 2022), known as Natalia LL, was a Polish artist. Her works were usually painted portraits, photography, drawings, performance and video art. She was a well known avant garde image making artist in Poland. In 1970 she co-founded PERMAFO, an artists' group and gallery.
She worked at the University of Fine Arts in Poznań from 2004 to 2013.
Natalia LL died on 12 August 2022 in Poznań, Poland at the age of 85.
