= = = Chautauqua, New York = = =
Chautauqua ( ) is a town and lake resort community in Chautauqua County, New York, United States. The population was 4,009 at the 2020 census. The town is named after Chautauqua Lake. It is the home of the Chautauqua Institution and the birthplace of the Chautauqua Movement.
The town formed from another, Batavia, on April 11, 1805, while still part of Genesee County.
= = = Peacock Princess = = =
The Peacock Princess or Chao Sisouthone and Nang Manola is a Tai legend. This story features in the folklore of Myanmar, Cambodia, Thailand, Laos, Sri Lanka, northern Malaysia, Indonesia, Vietnam and China.
= = = 2022 Oder environmental disaster = = =
The 2022 Oder environmental disaster occurred in August. Many fish, beavers and other wildlife in the Oder river in Poland and Germany died. This caused a health and environmental crisis.
On 11 August 2022, it was discovered that some parts of the Oder river were contaminated and many dead fish were seen on shore.
The discovery was made by local fishermen.
= = = 2022 Cetinje shooting = = =
On 12 August 2022, a mass shooting happened in Cetinje, Montenegro. A man killed ten people and injured six others. The shooting was caused by a fight between the shooter and people renting his home.
The gunman was Vučko Borilović. He was shot and killed by an armed civilian. It is the deadliest mass shooting in Montenegro's history.
= = = Vittorio De Sica = = =
