= = = Luis Enrique Oberto = = =
Luis Enrique Oberto González (19 August 1928 – 8 August 2022) was a Venezuelan banker and COPEI politician. He was the Minister of Finance from 1972 to 1974. He was a member of the Chamber of Deputies from 1979 to 1999. He was also the chamber president from 1990 to 1994. Oberto was born in Caracas, Venezuela.
Oberto died on 8 August 2022 in Caracas at the age of 93.
= = = David Tomassoni = = =
David Joseph Tomassoni (December 5, 1952 – August 11, 2022) was an American politician and ice hockey player. He was a member of the Minnesota Democratic–Farmer–Labor Party (DFL), however, Tomassoni left the party to become independent in November 2020. Tomassoni was born in Bemidji, Minnesota.
Tomassoni played ice hockey in Italy for 16 years and for the Italian national team at the 1984 Winter Olympics.
Tomassoni was a member of the Minnesota House of Representatives from 1993 to 2001. He later became a member of the Minnesota Senate from 2001 until his death. During his time in the senate, he was the Senate President from 2020 to 2021. He was state senate president pro tempore from 2021 to 2022.
In July 2021, Tomassoni announced he had been diagnosed with amyotrophic lateral sclerosis. He died from problems caused by the disease on August 11, 2022 under hospice care in Duluth, Minnesota at the age of 69.
= = = Togo Palazzi = = =
Togo Anthony Palazzi (August 8, 1932 – August 12, 2022) was an American basketball player. He played in the National Basketball Association (NBA) for the Boston Celtics and Syracuse Nationals between 1954 to 1960. Palazzi was born in Union City, New Jersey.
Palazzi died on August 12, 2022, four days after his 90th birthday.
= = = Vyacheslav Semyonov = = =
Vyacheslav Semyonov (, ; 18 August 1947 – 12 August 2022) was a Ukrainian footballer. He played as a midfielder or striker. He played for the Soviet Union national football team in 1972, making eleven appearances and four goals. He won a bronze medal at the 1972 Summer Olympics.
Semyonov died on 12 August 2022, six days before his 74th birthday.
= = = Piero Angela = = =
