Theia is a Titan in Greek mythology. It may also mean:
= = = Cable Music Channel = = =
The Cable Music Channel (CMC) was a short-lived American basic cable channel. It was owned by the Turner Broadcasting System.
= = = Sundanese language = = =
Sundanese () is a Malayo-Polynesian language. It is spoken by the Sundanese people.
Writing.
Sundanese is written with the Latin script, Sundanese script, or Pegon script. The Sundanese script is based on the Old Sundanese script. It was introduced in 1997. Pegon is based on the Arabic alphabet.
Phonology.
Vowels.
Sundanese has seven vowels.
Consonants.
Sundanese has eighteen consonants. There are also consonants such as and that are only used in loanwords.
= = = Sweet Charity (movie) = = =
Sweet Charity is a 1969 American romantic musical comedy-drama movie directed by first time director Bob Fosse and is based on the 1966 musical of the same name. It stars Shirley MacLaine, John McMartin, Paula Kelly, Chita Rivera, Barbara Bouchet, Sammy Davis Jr. and was distributed by Universal Pictures. It was nominated for 3 Academy Awards in 1970.
= = = 7food network = = =
7food network was a short-lived Australian free-to-air television channel. It was owned by the Seven Network which launched on 1 December 2018.
= = = Yosiwo George = = =
Yosiwo Palikkun George (July 24, 1941 – August 14, 2022) was the Vice President of the Federated States of Micronesia from 2015 until his death in 2022.
He served as Vice President under the presidencies of Peter M. Christian and David W. Panuelo. He served as Lieutenant Governor of Kosrae, Governor of Kosrae. He also was an Ambassador to the United States, Israel and the United Nations.
He died from COVID-19 on August 14, 2022 at the age of 81.
= = = Brimley's chorus frog = = =
The dismal swamp chorus frog or Brimley's chorus frog ("Pseudacris brimleyi") is a frog. It lives in the east coast of the United States, from Virginia to Georgia.
The adult male frog can be 30 mm long from nose to rear end and the adult female frog can be 35 mm long. The skin on the frog's back is light brown with lines in the middle and sides and a dark stripe from the eye to where the legs meet the body. There is a light colored line from the mouth to the ear. The skin of the belly is yellow-white in color.
= = = Associated Artists Productions = = =
Associated Artists Productions, Inc. (a.a.p.) later known as United Artists Associated was an American distributor of theatrical feature movies and subjects for television.
Through a series of acquisitions, Associated Artists Productions' assets have passed to Warner Bros. Discovery. Associated Artists Productions was the copyright owner of the "Popeye" shorts by Paramount Pictures, and the pre-1948 color "Looney Tunes" and "Merrie Melodies" series of shorts produced by Warner Bros..
= = = Beme (company) = = =
Beme Inc. () (pronounced as 'be me'), stylized as beme, was a multimedia company founded by Matt Hackett and Casey Neistat, a vlogger and short film maker on YouTube. Beme Inc. was the creator of the mobile app Beme. On November 28, 2016, CNN announced that it would acquire Beme. CNN intended to invest in the company and create a new brand focused on a young audience. The Beme app was officially shut down on January 31, 2017.
= = = Boomerang (Latin American TV channel) = = =
Boomerang was a 24-hour cable television channel. It is owned by Warner Bros. Discovery under its International division.
= = = Interstate 285 (Georgia) = = =
Interstate 285 (I-285) is an auxiliary Interstate Highway loop around Atlanta, Georgia, for . It connects three interstate highways to Atlanta: I-20, I-75 and I-85. The highway is also known as The Perimeter.
= = = Mottled duck = = =
The mottled duck ("Anas fulvigula") is a bird in the Anatidae family.
= = = Jacques Kyabula Katwe = = =
Jacques Kyabula Katwe was born on 13 March 1976 in the Democratic Republic of the Congo in the likasi city. He is the governor of the Haut-Katanga Province since 10 April 2019.
= = = Cornplanter = = =
John Abeel III or Gaiänt'wakê ("Gyantwachia" – "the planter") or Kaiiontwa'kon ("Kaintwakon" – "By What One Plants"), generally known as Cornplanter was a war chief of the Seneca tribe. He was also Dutch. His father was a Dutch trader, and his mother was a Seneca woman. He was born at Canawagus in New York. He fought in the French and Indian War and the American Revolutionary War. He initially wanted neutrality, but later was allied with the British. After the war, he was a negotiator between the Americans and Seneca people. He signed the Treaty of Fort Stanwix (1784), the Treaty of Fort Harmar (1789) and the Treaty of Canandaigua (1794) These treaties gave up Native land to the United States. Cornplanter invited Quakers to teach young Natives. Natives did not like this that much. Cornplanter believed that Natives should not resist whites. He also believed that Natives should peacefully give up lands. Many Natives were against his views. As a result, Red Jacket replaced Cornplanter as the Seneca leader. Conrplanter later got land in Pennsylvania and retired there.
= = = Brut Productions = = =
Brut Productions was a movie production company. It was an offshoot of Fabergé cosmetics under George Barrie.
= = = C4 (New Zealand TV channel) = = =
C4 was a New Zealand television channel. It was owned and operated by MediaWorks New Zealand.
= = = Canal 8 Sport = = =
