= = = Rossana Di Lorenzo = = =
Rossana Di Lorenzo (4 March 1938 – 13 August 2022) was an Italian actress. Her best known roles were in "Le coppie", "Il comune senso del pudore" and "Le Bal".
Lorenzo died on 13 August 2022 in Rome, Italy at the age of 84.
= = = Rodolfo Bebán = = =
Rodolfo Bebán (25 May 1938 – 14 August 2022) was an Argentine actor. He appeared in more than forty movies between 1962 and 2022. He was born in Ciudadela, Argentina. His best known roles were in "Arm in Arm Down the Street", "Hotel alojamiento", "Juan Moreira" and "El Fantástico mundo de María Montiel".
Bebán died on 14 August 2022, at the age of 84.
= = = Kristaq Dhamo = = =
Kristaq Dhamo (20 April 1933 – 14 August 2022) was an Albanian actor and movie director. His 1958 movie "Tana" was shown at the 1st Moscow International Film Festival. His career lasted from 1958 until 1987. He was born in Fier, Albania.
Dhamo died on 14 August 2022 at the age of 89.
= = = Svika Pick = = =
Zvika Pick (; 3 October 1949 – 14 August 2022) was a Polish-born Israeli pop singer-songwriter, composer, and television personality. He was born in Wrocław, Poland. He was known for writing songs that were contestants in the Eurovision Song Contest. These songs include "Diva" (1998), "Light a Candle" (2002) and "Hasta la Vista" (2003). He was also a musical judge on the reality show "Kokhav Nolad" from 2005 to 2009.
His daughter, Daniella Pick, married American director Quentin Tarantino in 2018.
Pick died on 14 August 2022 from cardiac arrest in Ramat HaSharon, Israel at the age of 72.
= = = Ramat HaSharon = = =
Ramat HaSharon (, "lit." "Sharon Heights" or "Heights of the (Great) Plain", ) is a city on Israel's central coastal section in the south of the Sharon region.
= = = Dmitri Vrubel = = =
Dmitri Vladimirovich Vrubel (; 14 July 1960 – 13 August 2022) was a Russian painter. He was best known for his painting "My God, Help Me to Survive This Deadly Love," which showed communist leaders Leonid Brezhnev and Erich Honecker kissing. This painting was graffiti on the Berlin Wall. He was born in Moscow.
Vrubel died on 14 August 2022, at the age of 62 from problems caused by COVID-19 at the age of 62.
= = = Academy of Television Arts &amp; Sciences = = =
The Academy of Television Arts &amp; Sciences (ATAS), also known as the Television Academy, is a professional honorary organization that focuses on the television industry in the United States. It is a 501(c)(6) non-profit organization. It was founded in 1946. It presents the Primetime Emmy Awards.
= = = Deadline Hollywood = = =
Deadline Hollywood, also known as Deadline and Deadline.com, is an online news site. It was founded as the news blog Deadline Hollywood Daily by Nikki Finke in 2006. The site is updated many times a day. They focus on entertainment news.
= = = IndieWire = = =
IndieWire is a movie business and review website. It was created in 1996. The site's focus was independent film. Today, however, it covers almost anything that is related to Hollywood such as popular movies, shows and celebrities.
= = = Playbill = = =
Playbill is a monthly U.S. magazine for theater fans. Most copies of "Playbill" are printed for specific stage productions and are given at the door as the show's program.
"Playbill" was first printed in 1884. The magazine is now used at nearly every Broadway theatre, as well as many Off-Broadway productions. Outside New York City, "Playbill" is used at theaters throughout the United States.
In September 2012, about 4,073,680 "Playbills" were made.
= = = Athabasca University = = =
Athabasca University (AU) is a Canadian public research university. It is mainly an online school. It was founded in 1970. It is one of the four academic and research universities in Alberta and was the first Canadian university to focus in distance education.
= = = Robert Fulford (journalist) = = =
Robert Marshall Blount Fulford (born February 13, 1932) is a Canadian journalist, magazine editor, and essayist. He was born in Ottawa, Ontario. He was a columnist for "The Toronto Star" from the 1950s to the 1970s. From 1963 to 1964 he was a columnist and editor of the Reviews section at "Maclean's" magazine.
= = = The Canadian Encyclopedia = = =
The Canadian Encyclopedia (TCE; ) is the national encyclopedia of Canada. It was published online by the Historica Canada. It also has the support of Canadian Heritage.
They are available for free online in both English and French. "The Canadian Encyclopedia" includes more than 19,500 articles in both languages about anything that is related to the country's history, culture, geography and entertainment areas.
= = = Elizabeth (biblical figure) = = =
Elizabeth (also spelled Elisabeth) was the mother of John the Baptist. She was the husband of Zechariah.
The angel Gabriel said to Zechariah that Elizabeth would have a son. Zechariah did not believe that his wife could have a son, because she was old. The angel made him mute (unable to speak). Elizabeth then became pregnant.
= = = Roberto Jefferson = = =
Roberto Jefferson Monteiro Francisco (born June 14, 1953) is a Brazilian politician. Jefferson was a member of the Chamber of Deputies from 1983 to 2005. He was removed from office over multiple corruption scandals. This banned him from being elected to any public office until 2015. He was a key figure of the Mensalão scandal.
His daughter is former Deputy Cristiane Brasil. He was born in Petrópolis, Brazil. He ran for President of Brazil in the 2022 election.
= = = Cristiane Brasil = = =
Cristiane Brasil Francisco, commonly known as Cristiane Brasil (born 21 December 1973), is a Brazilian lawyer and politician. She was a member of the Brazilian Labor Party (PTB). She was a Federal Deputy between 2015 and 2019.
Brasil was nominated as Minister of Labour in January 2018, but the Federal Justice suspended her nomination.
