= = = Strecker's chorus frog = = =
Strecker's chorus frog ("Pseudacris streckeri") is a frog. It lives in the United States. It lives in Oklahoma and parts of Kansas, Texas, and Louisiana. Scientists think it might also live in Utah.
This is the largest frog is the genus "Pseudacris". The adult can be 48 mm long from nose to rear end. The skin of the back may be brown, gray, or green. It has a dark stripe from its eyes to its body. It has dark spots on its back and a white belly. The skin where the back legs meet the body is orange-yellow in color.
This frog looks for food at night. During the day, it digs in the ground and hides under soil or wet leaves. Most frogs dig with their back legs, but this frog digs with its front legs.
This frog is not in danger of dying out but there are fewer of them than there were. This is because human beings build things in the places where the frog lives and cut down trees for wood. However, a subspecies of this frog, "Pseudacris streckeri illinoiensis", is endangered.
= = = Joseph Delaney = = =
Joseph Henry Delaney (25 July 1945 – 16 August 2022) was a British writer. He was known for his dark fantasy series "Spook's". Delaney was born in Preston, Lancashire.
Delaney died on 16 August 2022 at the age of 77.
= = = Niccolò Ghedini = = =
Niccolò Ghedini (22 December 1959 – 17 August 2022) was an Italian lawyer and politician. He was known as the lawyer of the former prime minister Silvio Berlusconi. Ghedini was a member of the Chamber of Deputies from 2001 to 2013. He also was a Senator from 2006 until his death. Ghedini was born in Padua, Italy.
Ghedini died on 17 August 2022 at a hospital in Milan, Italy from leukemia at the age of 62.
